    "body": "## Overview\n\nStreaming `/v1/completions` requests with `echo=true` put the full `prompt_token_ids` on the first chunk even when `return_token_ids` was not requested. This gates the field on `return_token_ids` in the echo branch, as the non-streaming response and the non-echo streaming branch already do (#27561 fixed the non-echo branch).\n\n## Claims\n\n- Streaming echo responses include `prompt_token_ids` only when `return_token_ids` is true, matching non-streaming responses.\n- No change when `return_token_ids` is true, or for non-echo requests.\n\n## Validation\n\nReal server on `34ac4f96a3` (Qwen3-0.6B, RTX 4090, `--enforce-eager`), streaming `{\"prompt\": \"Hello, my name is\", \"echo\": true, \"max_tokens\": 3, \"stream\": true}`. The table shows `prompt_token_ids` on the first chunk:\n\n| `return_token_ids` | `main` | this PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| unset | `[9707, 11, 847, 829, 374]` | `None` |\n| `true` | `[9707, 11, 847, 829, 374]` | `[9707, 11, 847, 829, 374]` |\n\nTests:\n\n- New `tests/entrypoints/openai/completion/test_completion_text_offset.py::test_stream_echo_returns_prompt_token_ids_only_on_request` (CPU, drives `completion_stream_generator` with a fake `RequestOutput`, like the existing test in that file). The `return_token_ids=False` case fails on `main` (`[9] == None`) and passes with the fix.\n- `pytest tests/entrypoints/openai/completion/test_completion_text_offset.py tests/entrypoints/openai/completion/test_completion_error.py tests/entrypoints/openai/completion/test_prompt_validation.py`: all pass.\n- `pre-commit run --files <changed files>`: all hooks pass.\n\n## Details\n\nIn `OpenAIServingCompletion.completion_stream_generator`, the echo branch set `prompt_token_ids_to_return = prompt_token_ids` unconditionally, while the non-echo branch next to it only does so when `request.return_token_ids` is set, and `request_output_to_completion_response` returns `prompt_token_ids` only on request. This moves the assignment under the existing `if request.return_token_ids:` in the echo branch. Besides being unrequested and inconsistent with non-streaming, the field repeats the whole prompt, which doubles the first chunk for long-prompt echo/scoring traffic.\n\nNot a duplicate: I found no issue or PR for this (searched \"echo prompt_token_ids stream\", \"return_token_ids echo streaming\", \"prompt_token_ids first chunk\"). #61660 edits this function for `echo` with `max_tokens=0` usage but not this line.\n\nAI assistance was used to find this bug, write the fix and the test, and run the validation shown above.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
